{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/489-hunter-what-do-you-think-it-should-be-called","id":489,"title":"Hunter: What Do You Think It Should Be Called?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-01T14:24:39-07:00","id":489,"title":"Hunter: What Do You Think It Should Be Called?","content":"There's this book. You've probably heard about it. The code name was Monstrous Basterds. <br /> <br /> We're not 100% settled on a title yet, so I figured, as part of Open Development, we'd drop it out there for you to weigh in. <br /> <br /> If you're unfamiliar, it's basically five micro-supplements, one for each of the games we have yet to cover in Hunter. There's a chapter on Promethean, one on Geist, one on Mummy, one on Changeling, and one on Demon. Then, we wrap it up with a whole fuckton of new Dread Powers and GMC updates for the Hunter core rules.<br /> <br /> Here's the three I'm looking at right now. I'm personally liking Remains, because it's a horror pun, but still sounds like a solid book title. Feel welcome to drop comments as well as poll responses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-01T14:47:35-07:00","id":532,"title":"","content":"I feel a bit stupid, but where do you actually click to vote?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and 